<speak>All right, the household sheet is aside. I'm staying with the notebook in front of me. There's one small scheduling preference for later: if we arrange an afternoon appointment, I'd rather not have it run into family dinner. I don't need an exact prediction for every call, just a reasonable block of time so I can plan around it. Today is comfortable because I've kept the afternoon open. It feels much better than trying to finish a conversation while someone is waiting at the door.</speak>